{"assets":["/statement-assets/c4c45cbaba96a290bca6e2be0f92c4773a91570a52dfb14e0acd6f4fab586e1c.png","/statement-assets/afae07b8b110d19a9eadb718bec5af2b822fce036e5f8a2a51c7f226aa1e4cde.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"261","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Maxim and Increasing Subsequence"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"6 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Maxim loves sequences, especially those that strictly increase. He is wondering, what is the length of the longest increasing subsequence of the given sequence "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Sequence "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":" is given as follows: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the length of the sequence equals "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n × t"},{"kind":"text","text":"; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/c4c45cbaba96a290bca6e2be0f92c4773a91570a52dfb14e0acd6f4fab586e1c.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1 ≤ i ≤ n × t)"},{"kind":"text","text":", where operation "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/afae07b8b110d19a9eadb718bec5af2b822fce036e5f8a2a51c7f226aa1e4cde.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" means taking the remainder after dividing number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":" by number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Sequence "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"s1,  s2,  ...,  sr"},{"kind":"text","text":" of length "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"r"},{"kind":"text","text":" is a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"subsequence"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of sequence "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a1,  a2,  ...,  an"},{"kind":"text","text":", if there is such increasing sequence of indexes "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i1, i2, ..., ir"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1  ≤  i1  <  i2  < ...   <  ir  ≤  n)"},{"kind":"text","text":", that "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"aij  =  sj"},{"kind":"text","text":". In other words, the subsequence can be obtained from the sequence by crossing out some elements."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Sequence "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"s1,  s2,  ...,  sr"},{"kind":"text","text":" is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"increasing"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", if the following inequality holds: "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"s1 < s2 <  ... <  sr"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Maxim have "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" variants of the sequence "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":". Help Maxim to determine for each sequence the length of the longest increasing subsequence."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains four integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"maxb"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"t"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1 ≤ k ≤ 10; 1 ≤ n, maxb ≤ 105; 1 ≤ t ≤ 109; n × maxb ≤ 2·107)"},{"kind":"text","text":". Each of the next "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines contain "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b1, b2, ..., bn"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1 ≤ bi ≤ maxb)"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that for each variant of the sequence "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":" the values "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"maxb"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"t"},{"kind":"text","text":" coincide, the only arrays "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b"},{"kind":"text","text":"s differ."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The numbers in the lines are separated by single spaces."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers — the answers for the variants of the sequence "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":". Print the answers in the order the variants follow in the input."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3 3 5 2\n3 2 1\n1 2 3\n2 3 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2\n3\n3\n"}],"kind